2026-10-20T13:23:33.6772560Z CLANG_CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_DIR: /opt/homebrew/etc/clang
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6773170Z CLANG_CONFIG_FILE_USER_DIR:   ~/.config/clang
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6773410Z 
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6773690Z LLD and LLDB are now provided in separate formulae:
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6774080Z   brew install lld
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6776290Z   brew install lldb
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6776440Z 
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6777570Z Z3 solver support will be removed in LLVM 24 as it is unsupported upstream,
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6780320Z see https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/205370
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6780960Z 
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6781350Z Using `clang`, `clang++`, etc., requires a CLT installation at `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools`.
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6783210Z If you don't want to install the CLT, you can write appropriate configuration files pointing to your
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6784730Z SDK at ~/.config/clang.
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6784920Z 
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6785790Z To use the bundled libunwind please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6786300Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6786570Z 
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6786830Z To use the bundled libc++ please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6788410Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/c++ -L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6789210Z Features newer than system libc++ will require the following define to enable
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6790060Z (support for this may be removed in a future major LLVM release):
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6790550Z   CPPFLAGS="-D_LIBCPP_DISABLE_AVAILABILITY"
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6790760Z 
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6791250Z NOTE: You probably want to use the libunwind and libc++ provided by macOS unless you know what you're doing.
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6791710Z 
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6792010Z llvm is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6793450Z because macOS already provides this software and installing another version in
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6795580Z parallel can cause all kinds of trouble.
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6795790Z 
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6796000Z If you need to have llvm first in your PATH, run:
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6796880Z   echo 'export PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:$PATH"' >> /Users/runner/.bash_profile
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6797190Z 
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6797410Z For compilers to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6799200Z   export LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib"
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6799660Z   export CPPFLAGS="-I/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/include"
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6800500Z 
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6801470Z For cmake to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-10-20T13:23:33.6802350Z   export CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm"
